    "evidence_text": "Dear Heart (song)\n\n It appears on the 1965 Andy Williams album, \"Andy Williams' Dear Heart\".\n\nIt's the Most Wonderful Time of the Year\n\n It was recorded and released that year by pop singer Andy Williams for his first Christmas album, \"The Andy Williams Christmas Album\".\n\nWe Need a Little Christmas (album)\n\n I felt like I was singing them for the very first time.\"\n\nAndy Williams' Greatest Hits\n\nAndy Williams Sings Steve Allen\n\nHark! The Herald Angels Sing\n\n\"Hark!\n\n Wesley had requested and received slow and solemn music for his lyrics, not the joyful tune expected today.\n\n Moreover, Wesley's original opening couplet is \"Hark!\n\n how all the welkin rings / Glory to the King of Kings\".\n\nGet Together with Andy Williams\n\n The one new song was \"You Are\", which was written by Mac Davis.\n\nSo Soon in the Morning\n\n The duo sung it in a fast gospel tempo.\n\nCorcovado (song)\n\n An English lyric was later written by Gene Lees.\n\n Also receiving air-play, contemporaneously with Andy Williams' recording of \"Quiet Nights,\" was Kitty Kallen's version.\n\nHawaiian Wedding Song",
